WEBVTT

00:02.520 --> 00:07.190
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

00:07.190 --> 00:11.520
<i>Charging at full speed, straight ahead</i>

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:11.520 --> 00:13.330
<i>That's how I live</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:29.750
<i>I keep turning them over in my mind</i>

00:29.750 --> 00:32.720
<i>All the things I want to do</i>

00:32.720 --> 00:39.970
<i>Even if I'm told that's not 
what's expected of me</i>

00:39.970 --> 00:43.310
<i>I don't plan on giving them up</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:51.870
<i>Ah, dreams are meant to be big</i>

00:51.870 --> 00:56.840
<i>I'll head where the shining coin points me</i>

00:56.840 --> 01:01.870
<i>And nothing can stop me</i>

01:01.870 --> 01:07.000
<i>I won't back down, I'll face forward</i>

01:07.000 --> 01:12.250
<i>So I can fulfill my dream</i>

01:12.550 --> 01:17.180
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:21.560
<i>Wind at my back, giving it my all</i>

01:21.560 --> 01:23.300
<i>That's how I live</i>

01:32.400 --> 01:34.410
Thank you for your business!

01:35.520 --> 01:36.700
Yep!

01:36.700 --> 01:41.650
Sales of shampoo, shampoo, and 
shampoo are through the roof as always!

01:41.650 --> 01:44.550
I owe it all to those three!

01:44.550 --> 01:48.790
Okay! Time to keep it up and 
rake in loads and loads of moolah!

01:49.330 --> 01:56.050
For that, I think I need another hot-selling 
"it" product, aside from shampoo...

01:56.530 --> 02:00.040
<i>Well, I messed up a teensy bit before...</i>

02:01.420 --> 02:03.310
Welcome!

02:09.280 --> 02:11.400
<i>Oh!</i>

02:11.400 --> 02:12.770
<i>She's drop-dead gorgeous!</i>

02:13.630 --> 02:15.010
Excuse me...

02:15.010 --> 02:17.990
Would this happen to be 
General Store Mitsuha?

02:17.990 --> 02:20.990
Mitsuha Visits the Royal Palace

02:21.350 --> 02:23.760
I came to visit because I'd heard of

02:23.760 --> 02:26.670
an interesting shop stocked 
with all sorts of curious goods.

02:26.670 --> 02:28.500
Ah, yes! This is the place!

02:28.500 --> 02:31.890
What a relief. I didn't see a sign outside...

02:31.890 --> 02:32.950
A sign!

02:32.950 --> 02:35.450
<i>Oh! I forgot I didn't have one!</i>

02:35.450 --> 02:39.790
<i>Is that the reason I didn't get 
any customers in the beginning?!</i>

02:39.790 --> 02:42.890
<i>Sheesh! How come no one 
said anything to me?!</i>

02:43.410 --> 02:45.630
Please allow me to peruse 
your offerings, then.

02:45.630 --> 02:47.430
Yes, please help yourself!

02:47.880 --> 02:50.350
<i>She's giving off some aristocratic vibes...</i>

02:50.780 --> 02:53.400
<i>The very image of dignity and grace...</i>

02:53.400 --> 02:58.500
<i>And most importantly, her stunning 
beauty that just screams princess!</i>

02:59.820 --> 03:01.580
<i>A real sight for sore eyes!</i>

03:05.150 --> 03:07.690
I'll be purchasing these, 
and some shampoo, as well.

03:08.920 --> 03:10.580
<i>Buying in bulk, I see!</i>

03:10.580 --> 03:12.570
<i>And shampoo for her as well!</i>

03:13.450 --> 03:15.500
Will this suffice as payment?

03:15.780 --> 03:18.320
Y-Yes, that's enough.

03:18.320 --> 03:22.510
<i>Hmm... Paying with gold 
without batting an eyelid...</i>

03:22.510 --> 03:25.510
<i>No security detail with her? Really?</i>

03:26.060 --> 03:27.510
Thanks for your patience!

03:27.510 --> 03:29.380
Ah, the bag is on the house!

03:29.380 --> 03:30.870
Oh, how charming!

03:30.870 --> 03:32.940
I really enjoyed myself! I'll be back!

03:32.940 --> 03:34.150
<i>That means a repeat customer!</i>

03:35.470 --> 03:37.490
Thank you for your purchase!

03:38.920 --> 03:40.190
<i>Over there...</i>

03:40.620 --> 03:41.900
<i>How shady-looking!</i>

03:41.900 --> 03:45.160
<i>He's just asking to be 
taken away by the police!</i>

03:45.480 --> 03:49.120
<i>Is he after me... or maybe the shop?</i>

03:51.190 --> 03:53.250
<i>Guess I was wrong.</i>

03:54.540 --> 03:57.380
<i>Wait, it was the girl instead!</i>

03:59.800 --> 04:03.090
<i>I've learned from last time 
and prepared for this!</i>

04:03.450 --> 04:06.850
<i>Things will get messy if 
an aristocratic lady disappears</i>

04:06.850 --> 04:09.220
<i>after last being seen 
at General Store Mitsuha!</i>

04:11.740 --> 04:12.680
<i>Bingo!</i>

04:16.060 --> 04:17.110
<i>Partners in crime!</i>

04:18.980 --> 04:20.650
What are you doing?!

04:20.980 --> 04:23.210
Huh? Who do you think <i>you</i> are?

04:23.210 --> 04:25.910
A friend of hers? How heroic of you.

04:25.910 --> 04:28.000
<i>Abducting her for ransom?</i>

04:28.000 --> 04:29.920
<i>Or human trafficking?</i>

04:30.520 --> 04:32.000
<i>I can't just look the other way!</i>

04:32.000 --> 04:35.250
Hmm? Gonna fight back?

04:36.960 --> 04:39.820
Put on a brave front all you like, missy,

04:39.820 --> 04:41.260
but can you take a person's life?

04:45.800 --> 04:47.240
I sure can.

04:47.870 --> 04:51.140
Is there any reason 
I shouldn't kill a lowlife?

04:54.100 --> 04:56.300
<i>Well, I didn't kill anyone.</i>

04:56.300 --> 04:58.560
<i>This is a pistol-type stun gun.</i>

04:59.870 --> 05:01.790
Who the hell <i>are</i> you?!

05:02.370 --> 05:04.270
<i>I'm glad you asked!</i>

05:04.270 --> 05:06.560
<i>I'll bluster and bluff my way 
through this situation!</i>

05:06.560 --> 05:08.990
<i>Time for me to summon my cringe-worthy past!</i>

05:09.790 --> 05:10.870
Who am I?

05:11.660 --> 05:15.080
They call me... the Messenger.

05:15.800 --> 05:16.990
Huh?

05:16.990 --> 05:19.740
<i>Their faces are like, 
"What the hell is she saying?"</i>

05:19.740 --> 05:23.420
<i>Yeah, I get it! I don't know 
what I'm saying, either!</i>

05:23.870 --> 05:28.220
<i>But now's my chance to bust out my list 
of lines I've always wanted to say out loud!</i>

05:28.640 --> 05:31.130
I am the Messenger of Lightning!

05:31.130 --> 05:33.180
I'll show no mercy to those 
who bare their blades!

05:39.020 --> 05:39.860
Run for it!

05:39.860 --> 05:40.660
What?!

05:41.370 --> 05:42.430
Soldiers?!

05:42.430 --> 05:44.530
We're done for!

05:44.530 --> 05:46.410
Don't hurt me!

05:50.830 --> 05:51.710
Princess!

05:51.710 --> 05:53.540
Princess! Princess!

05:53.540 --> 05:55.440
Oh, the poor thing!

05:55.440 --> 05:56.790
I'm begging you!

05:56.790 --> 06:00.920
Please stop running away from 
your bodyguards, Princess!

06:00.920 --> 06:04.220
Oh? Did a single young girl 
prove too elusive for you?

06:04.220 --> 06:07.220
A display unbecoming 
of the honorable Royal Guards!

06:07.220 --> 06:10.890
<i>Hmm? So she really was a princess?</i>

06:10.890 --> 06:12.490
<i>Is that so?</i>

06:12.490 --> 06:14.180
Please wait, dear Messenger!

06:15.560 --> 06:19.060
Er... just how much did you hear?

06:19.060 --> 06:22.440
That would be from when you 
said, "What are you doing?"

06:23.030 --> 06:24.950
<i>From the very start? Is that right?</i>

06:24.950 --> 06:27.030
<i>Thanks for letting me know!</i>

06:27.340 --> 06:30.240
Please spare me. I'm sorry. 
I got carried away.

06:28.510 --> 06:30.240
Dear Messenger?

06:30.880 --> 06:32.560
Please join us at the Royal Palace.

06:32.560 --> 06:34.370
<i>That's how it goes, huh?</i>

06:45.130 --> 06:47.600
Art thou the one who goes by Mitsuha?

06:47.600 --> 06:49.300
I am...

06:49.300 --> 06:50.710
You saved my daughter.

06:50.710 --> 06:53.800
No need for formalities. Please be at ease.

06:54.880 --> 06:55.870
Take a seat.

06:55.870 --> 06:56.950
Yes!

06:56.950 --> 07:02.800
Why, I just wanted to offer my gratitude 
as a father for saving my daughter.

07:02.800 --> 07:05.020
I'll spare you the customary 
manner of speech, as well.

07:05.020 --> 07:07.700
<i>I see. That makes sense.</i>

07:07.700 --> 07:11.280
<i>This isn't a formal audience 
or an investiture.</i>

07:11.280 --> 07:14.640
So, Miss Mitsuha, 
the Messenger of Lightning.

07:14.640 --> 07:16.740
I'm Mitsuha, general store owner.

07:17.370 --> 07:20.500
So, Miss Mitsuha, 
the Messenger of Lightning.

07:20.500 --> 07:22.620
I'm Mitsuha, general store owner.

07:22.620 --> 07:25.130
Miss Mitsuha, the Messenger of Lightning!

07:25.580 --> 07:27.420
I'm Mitsuha, general store owner!

07:27.420 --> 07:28.440
Miss Mitsuha, the Mess—

07:28.440 --> 07:30.380
I'm Mitsuha, general store owner!

07:31.780 --> 07:33.940
Miss Mitsuha, general store owner.

07:33.940 --> 07:34.850
<i>I've won!</i>

07:36.010 --> 07:37.250
Yes.

07:37.250 --> 07:40.540
As I was seeing Her Highness off 
after shopping at my establishment,

07:40.540 --> 07:44.550
I caught sight of a suspicious man, 
and followed him out of concern.

07:44.550 --> 07:46.760
And what do I see but an abduction!

07:47.500 --> 07:51.650
I gathered my courage and called out 
to them, yet I am but a young lady.

07:52.090 --> 07:56.990
It was then, in the nick of time, 
that the guards showed up and saved us!

07:56.990 --> 08:00.510
Hmm... that's quite 
a different story than I was told.

08:01.000 --> 08:02.200
Well, no matter.

08:02.200 --> 08:05.660
In any case, let me offer my 
thanks for saving my daughter.

08:05.660 --> 08:07.380
Go on and thank her.

08:08.580 --> 08:10.210
My name is Sabine.

08:10.210 --> 08:13.930
<i>Oh! So this cute little angel 
goes by Sabine!</i>

08:13.930 --> 08:17.180
Lady Mitsuha, thank you 
very much for saving me!

08:17.180 --> 08:21.680
Your Highness, you really shouldn't 
be addressing a commoner as "Lady"!

08:21.680 --> 08:25.150
Oh, but I owe my life to you!

08:25.150 --> 08:27.920
We're fortunate that you were unharmed.

08:27.920 --> 08:31.230
I'll need to have a stern word 
with you later, Sabine.

08:31.230 --> 08:33.800
Slipping past the guards and 
sneaking out of the castle...

08:33.800 --> 08:35.320
I'm sorry...

08:35.320 --> 08:37.820
But you're about to put an end

08:37.820 --> 08:40.450
to that pesky human trafficking 
ring as a result, aren't you?

08:40.450 --> 08:44.360
Don't you feel that I deserve 
a pardon from your lecturing, Father?

08:45.330 --> 08:48.460
The lady's maids were gossiping 
about General Store Mitsuha,

08:48.460 --> 08:50.730
so I just had to go and see for myself!

08:50.730 --> 08:52.880
It was quite an amusing place.

08:52.880 --> 08:54.590
So is it fine for me to visit again?

08:54.590 --> 08:56.980
Please, Father!

08:59.710 --> 09:00.730
Miss Mitsuha.

09:00.730 --> 09:01.520
Yes?

09:01.520 --> 09:04.750
Please continue to treat my children kindly.

09:04.750 --> 09:06.120
<i>Eh?!</i>

09:06.120 --> 09:08.180
I'm Rouven, the second prince.

09:08.180 --> 09:10.850
I hope we can get along, Lady Mitsuha.

09:10.850 --> 09:12.530
S-Sure...

09:12.780 --> 09:16.910
<i>Hmm, this has turned into 
a bit of a hairy situation...</i>

09:16.910 --> 09:18.550
<i>Oh, that's right.</i>

09:18.550 --> 09:23.620
Your Majesty, have you found that your 
sight's gotten worse from your days of youth?

09:23.620 --> 09:27.780
Yes. I find it hard to read 
the minuscule text on documents.

09:27.780 --> 09:29.380
So I use a lens...

09:29.380 --> 09:31.410
<i>What? They have reading glasses?</i>

09:31.410 --> 09:33.570
<i>That's more advanced than I thought!</i>

09:34.490 --> 09:35.260
<i>I see!</i>

09:35.260 --> 09:37.550
<i>Reading glasses use convex lenses,</i>

09:37.550 --> 09:41.470
<i>and were adopted much earlier than 
concave lenses were to treat myopia!</i>

09:41.470 --> 09:47.230
<i>But I believe early glasses were single, 
handheld lenses or pince-nez eyeglasses.</i>

09:47.230 --> 09:48.050
<i>Whatever!</i>

09:48.050 --> 09:50.430
<i>Even if this world has reading glasses,</i>

09:50.430 --> 09:53.460
<i>I'm sure they're no match 
for modern Earth ones!</i>

09:54.110 --> 09:56.900
Reading 
Glasses

09:54.110 --> 09:56.900
Reading 
Glasses

09:54.110 --> 09:56.900
Reading 
Glasses

09:54.110 --> 09:56.900
Reading 
Glasses

09:54.110 --> 09:56.900
Could I have you try these on for size?

09:57.280 --> 09:58.980
You wear them like this.

09:58.980 --> 10:02.530
They're all different, so please find 
the one that lets you see best.

10:02.530 --> 10:04.590
Hmm? Like this?

10:05.700 --> 10:08.390
Oh! How lightweight these are!

10:08.390 --> 10:10.080
And I can see so clearly!

10:10.390 --> 10:12.340
Come, Sahr! Try putting these on!

10:12.340 --> 10:14.360
Yes! If you'll pardon me...

10:16.230 --> 10:17.840
Oh!

10:17.840 --> 10:22.660
I recall that you'd found handheld lenses 
and eyeglasses difficult to use.

10:22.660 --> 10:23.980
How about these?

10:23.980 --> 10:27.660
These are a far cry from other lenses, 
and everything's so clear!

10:27.660 --> 10:29.110
I know, right?

10:29.110 --> 10:32.810
This should make looking 
over documents much easier.

10:32.810 --> 10:37.570
It seems that I, Sahr, won't be stepping 
down as chancellor any time soon!

10:37.570 --> 10:41.530
<i>Ah, so he's the chancellor? Is that right?</i>

10:41.530 --> 10:43.820
<i>I've found the perfect person 
to endorse my products!</i>

10:43.820 --> 10:46.540
<i>Good thing I brought those reading glasses!</i>

10:46.880 --> 10:49.230
Mitsuha, do you have anything else?

10:49.230 --> 10:50.860
Please show me your best items!

10:50.860 --> 10:52.790
Naturally, I'll make sure to pay for them!

10:53.180 --> 10:55.430
Well, sure. That's how we do business.

10:55.430 --> 10:56.850
As long as you pay for it,

10:56.850 --> 11:00.130
General Store Mitsuha's here 
to sell you whatever you'd like!

11:00.540 --> 11:01.640
However...

11:02.180 --> 11:04.390
The one exception is women.

11:06.830 --> 11:08.520
No women, you say?

11:08.520 --> 11:10.010
No can do!

11:10.010 --> 11:11.180
I see!

11:17.860 --> 11:23.410
So she meant, "No matter how much money 
you offer, I won't do your bidding"...

11:23.760 --> 11:25.770
The Messenger of Lightning...

11:27.250 --> 11:30.400
Sahr, have that girl looked into.

11:30.400 --> 11:31.580
Yes!

11:34.280 --> 11:36.960
<i>I'm glad that I was able to sell them 
on the reading glasses...</i>

11:36.960 --> 11:38.680
<i>I'm glad, but...</i>

11:39.210 --> 11:43.190
<i>Ah! Why'd I get carried away 
and give myself that name?!</i>

11:43.190 --> 11:46.600
<i>Another page added to my cringe-worthy past!</i>

11:47.120 --> 11:51.270
<i>I just hope it doesn't get 
me in any weird trouble...</i>

12:02.520 --> 12:03.530
Wow!

12:11.700 --> 12:13.410
Welcome...

12:14.830 --> 12:17.530
<i>Ah... this guy means trouble...</i>

12:17.960 --> 12:20.960
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:20.960 --> 12:23.970
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

12:25.220 --> 12:26.930
Are you the owner here?

12:27.410 --> 12:30.180
Hand over the deed to this shop 
and your supply chains!

12:30.180 --> 12:32.520
<i>Yikes! What's with him?!</i>

12:32.520 --> 12:36.180
Hmm... I think I'll take you in for myself.

12:36.180 --> 12:37.420
<i>Blech!</i>

12:37.420 --> 12:40.230
Er... exactly who might you be?

12:40.230 --> 12:41.530
What's this now?!

12:41.530 --> 12:42.850
You don't know who I am?!

12:42.850 --> 12:46.150
This is why little girls 
have no place running a store!

12:46.740 --> 12:49.240
That's fine. Let me tell you who I am.

12:49.240 --> 12:52.920
I am the president of the Adler Trading 
Company, which holds a royal warrant,

12:52.920 --> 12:54.710
Nelson Adler!

12:54.710 --> 12:57.830
Oh! The Adler Trading Company!

12:57.830 --> 12:59.660
<i>Never heard of it!</i>

12:59.660 --> 13:03.360
<i>Well, if he's president, that must 
mean he's the company head.</i>

13:03.360 --> 13:09.590
It seems this shop deals in unusual items, 
such as fresh fish and shampoo.

13:09.590 --> 13:12.470
You show some signs of promise, 
despite your young age.

13:12.810 --> 13:15.980
I'll be taking over for you, 
so show some gratitude!

13:16.500 --> 13:19.190
<i>Uh-huh, so that's what you're here for.</i>

13:19.190 --> 13:23.560
<i>The count's authority doesn't 
extend to merchants, I see.</i>

13:24.260 --> 13:26.690
Um... if that's the case,

13:26.690 --> 13:29.600
could you come visit us 
tomorrow at the same time?

13:29.600 --> 13:32.530
I'll ask my business partner 
to come, as well.

13:33.370 --> 13:36.830
I see. Then, I'll take my leave for now.

13:37.890 --> 13:39.730
I look forward to your visit.

13:56.980 --> 13:58.980
Yamano

13:59.810 --> 14:02.150
I'm here, Elder Sister Mitsuha!

14:02.150 --> 14:03.680
You're back!

14:04.240 --> 14:07.730
<i>Sabine's visited almost every day since then.</i>

14:07.730 --> 14:09.380
<i>Practically a regular flight.</i>

14:09.380 --> 14:11.350
<i>Incidentally, after several twists and turns,</i>

14:11.350 --> 14:14.490
<i>she settled on calling me 
"Elder Sister Mitsuha".</i>

14:15.340 --> 14:16.520
Lady Mitsuha!

14:16.620 --> 14:17.700
Lady Mitsuha!

14:17.850 --> 14:19.710
Lady Mitsuha!

14:19.970 --> 14:22.370
Please don't call me that! 
My neck is on the line!

14:22.370 --> 14:23.790
Eh?

14:27.010 --> 14:28.680
More of the dee vee dee!

14:28.680 --> 14:30.810
Elder Sister Mitsuha, hurry, hurry!

14:30.810 --> 14:31.850
Sure thing.

14:32.310 --> 14:36.810
<i>I messed up and now she knows about DVDs...</i>

14:36.810 --> 14:37.970
What's this?

14:37.970 --> 14:38.880
Whoa!

14:38.880 --> 14:40.790
Ah! Are you okay?!

14:40.790 --> 14:41.400
Ah...

14:41.400 --> 14:41.900
PLAYER

14:43.380 --> 14:46.490
What is this? What is this? What <i>is</i> this?!

14:47.090 --> 14:48.010
Listen to me.

14:48.010 --> 14:52.230
I've said this before, but this is 
a magic mirror that shows faraway events.

14:52.230 --> 14:55.530
If you speak of this to anyone, 
it'll shatter on the spot!

14:55.530 --> 14:56.530
So be careful!

14:56.530 --> 14:57.870
Yes, Elder Sister Mitsuha!

14:59.260 --> 15:01.780
Also, before I forget...

15:01.780 --> 15:02.880
Here, take this.

15:02.880 --> 15:05.940
Could you hand it over to 
the chancellor as soon as you go back?

15:05.940 --> 15:09.330
It's a very important letter, 
so you mustn't forget.

15:10.640 --> 15:11.420
Yeah!

15:11.420 --> 15:13.890
I'll make sure I deliver it, 
so Elder Sister Mitsuha...

15:13.890 --> 15:14.850
Here you go!

15:15.810 --> 15:17.720
Right away, Princess...

15:18.410 --> 15:20.930
<i>Sabine doesn't understand Japanese,</i>

15:20.930 --> 15:23.900
<i>so I have to dub over a translation for her!</i>

15:24.340 --> 15:26.480
You corrupted bandwagon normies!

15:26.480 --> 15:28.400
Go back to being otaku at once!

15:28.810 --> 15:31.820
Elder Sister Mitsuha! 
Put some more feeling into it!

15:31.820 --> 15:33.480
Do the poses, as well!

15:33.480 --> 15:35.690
<i>You've gotta be kidding...</i>

15:44.000 --> 15:45.340
Hey, girlie!

15:45.340 --> 15:47.240
I've brought the assignment 
agreement with me!

15:47.240 --> 15:48.880
Hurry up and sign it!

15:49.290 --> 15:52.880
<i>Mister Nelson's as impatient 
as ever, right from the get-go!</i>

15:53.580 --> 15:56.390
Elder Sister Mitsuha, who's this?

15:57.070 --> 16:01.680
He's a big shot from a large trading 
company who said he wants to take me in.

16:01.680 --> 16:02.640
What?!

16:02.640 --> 16:05.420
I don't want you to leave, 
Elder Sister Mitsuha!

16:05.420 --> 16:08.110
<i>Sabine's a great actress!</i>

16:08.110 --> 16:11.060
If you want to be with your sister so badly,

16:11.060 --> 16:13.820
I can take you in, as well, little missy.

16:13.820 --> 16:14.910
Really?

16:14.910 --> 16:17.160
Yes. Would I lie to you?

16:17.160 --> 16:20.000
I'll take both of you and...

16:20.000 --> 16:21.680
Wh-What now?!

16:21.680 --> 16:24.370
My apologies! 
Hope I didn't keep you waiting!

16:24.370 --> 16:26.170
Ch-Chancellor!

16:26.170 --> 16:28.850
Sorry to have you come all this way, Sahr.

16:28.850 --> 16:30.380
S-Sahr?!

16:30.380 --> 16:31.620
Not at all!

16:31.620 --> 16:35.050
Just say the word, Miss Mitsuha, 
and I'll be at your service!

16:35.050 --> 16:37.720
<i>She's on a first-name basis 
with the chancellor?!</i>

16:37.720 --> 16:40.100
<i>Not to mention his obsequious demeanor!</i>

16:40.100 --> 16:41.520
<i>What's going on here?!</i>

16:41.920 --> 16:46.290
You see, this man wants me to 
relinquish this shop at no cost to him.

16:46.290 --> 16:50.780
He also said he wanted to take 
custody of the both of us...

16:50.780 --> 16:55.410
It looks like I have no choice but 
to turn down His Majesty's request...

16:57.260 --> 17:00.950
What exactly is the meaning 
of this, Mister Adler?!

17:00.950 --> 17:04.170
Huh? No, well...

17:04.170 --> 17:09.160
Harassment and obstruction of a merchant 
under direct contract for His Royal Highness.

17:09.160 --> 17:12.210
Unlawful bidding for an 
establishment without recompense.

17:12.540 --> 17:15.410
Coercing juvenile girls into one's own custody.

17:15.410 --> 17:16.790
Does that sum it all up?

17:16.790 --> 17:19.680
Huh? Oh no, I-I wouldn't dream of...

17:19.680 --> 17:21.370
You wouldn't dream of such a thing?

17:21.370 --> 17:23.890
N-No! That goes without saying!

17:23.890 --> 17:28.650
So going forward, you won't meddle 
with this store or its proprietor,

17:28.650 --> 17:31.210
directly or otherwise?

17:31.210 --> 17:33.150
Yes, I swear it on the gods!

17:33.150 --> 17:34.560
Very well.

17:34.560 --> 17:38.660
In that case, if I find any obstruction 
of this business in the future,

17:38.660 --> 17:42.450
you will be the one held fully 
responsible, Mister Adler.

17:42.450 --> 17:45.400
It is your duty to properly 
inform everyone at your company.

17:45.400 --> 17:47.870
Y-Yes! You can leave it to me!

17:48.590 --> 17:52.000
<i>With this, the Adler 
Trading Company became liable</i>

17:52.000 --> 17:54.250
<i>for monitoring all 
the merchants in the capital,</i>

17:54.250 --> 17:57.280
<i>to make sure they didn't meddle 
with General Store Mitsuha.</i>

17:57.280 --> 18:00.420
<i>If they overlook or leave 
unattended any such obstruction,</i>

18:00.420 --> 18:03.600
<i>who knows what consequences they might face?</i>

18:05.080 --> 18:06.200
Oh, in addition...

18:06.200 --> 18:06.890
Yes?

18:06.890 --> 18:08.970
Starting tomorrow, we will no longer need

18:08.970 --> 18:12.120
Adler Trading Company 
representatives in the palace.

18:12.120 --> 18:15.700
All regular entry permits 
are hereby revoked.

18:15.700 --> 18:16.400
What?!

18:16.400 --> 18:18.640
W-Wait a minute, Chancellor Sahr!

18:18.640 --> 18:20.700
What's this all of a sudden?

18:20.700 --> 18:22.560
Why, it's only natural.

18:22.560 --> 18:25.050
As gracious as His Royal Majesty may be,

18:25.050 --> 18:29.980
he would never allow 
palace entry again to someone

18:29.980 --> 18:32.380
who tried to make away with his daughter.

18:32.380 --> 18:34.710
Huh? H-His daughter?

18:34.710 --> 18:36.420
Eh?

18:36.840 --> 18:38.380
Eh?!

18:46.250 --> 18:47.180
Ah...

18:47.180 --> 18:49.140
Ahh!

18:49.460 --> 18:52.460
Come, let us return, 
Your Royal Highness Sabine.

18:52.460 --> 18:56.860
What?! I want to play some more 
with Elder Sister Mitsuha!

18:56.860 --> 18:58.820
No!

18:58.820 --> 19:00.640
P-Prez!

19:00.640 --> 19:02.590
Get a hold of yourself!

19:02.590 --> 19:05.330
<i>The resignation of the Adler 
Trading Company president,</i>

19:05.330 --> 19:07.670
<i>followed by his son's complete succession,</i>

19:07.670 --> 19:11.000
<i>would come to take place some time after.</i>

19:11.000 --> 19:15.680
Keep your hands off General Store Mitsuha!

19:18.110 --> 19:21.430
This past case has really 
proved to be a godsend.

19:21.430 --> 19:23.440
Yes, most certainly.

19:23.440 --> 19:27.000
So, what of those in contact 
with the Adler Trading Company

19:27.000 --> 19:30.770
who were after knowledge of palace workings?

19:30.770 --> 19:32.340
We had captured them,

19:32.340 --> 19:35.510
but they all took poison, so we 
still don't know the finer details.

19:35.510 --> 19:37.030
My deepest apologies.

19:37.770 --> 19:40.490
So they chose to take their own lives...

19:40.490 --> 19:41.750
Be that as it may,

19:41.750 --> 19:46.200
we've managed to rid the palace 
of the Adler Trading Company,

19:46.200 --> 19:48.370
which has been a hotbed of corruption.

19:48.370 --> 19:51.160
Taking inadequate measures 
would have invited backlash.

19:51.160 --> 19:52.990
Now we have a suitable pretext.

19:52.990 --> 19:56.740
Miss Mitsuha has sent 
a courteous letter of gratitude.

19:56.740 --> 20:00.260
But it seems we should be 
the ones thanking her.

20:01.450 --> 20:06.470
If this were a matter that could be 
made public, I would have been happy to.

20:06.470 --> 20:12.130
But to have a human trafficking ring 
committing crimes in broad daylight...

20:12.130 --> 20:13.890
Something doesn't add up.

20:14.480 --> 20:16.730
There may be more to this than we know.

20:16.730 --> 20:21.090
I'll continue investigating 
into both these matters.

20:21.090 --> 20:23.320
While remaining vigilant.

20:23.640 --> 20:26.800
Yes. If it turns out to be nothing, 
then all the better.

20:27.530 --> 20:30.100
What could be better than peace?

20:32.490 --> 20:33.540
I must say, though...

20:33.540 --> 20:36.340
I'm surprised at how she 
saved Her Royal Highness,

20:36.340 --> 20:41.310
as well as leading Adler 
by the nose so effortlessly.

20:41.310 --> 20:42.380
I completely agree.

20:42.920 --> 20:47.600
That girl Mitsuha... 
she fascinates me more than ever.

20:47.600 --> 20:49.310
Achoo!

20:50.370 --> 20:51.940
I hope it's not a cold...

20:51.940 --> 20:53.460
Elder Sister Mitsuha!

20:53.460 --> 20:56.000
Show me more of the dee vee dee!

20:56.000 --> 20:57.310
Sure thing...

20:57.310 --> 21:00.530
Men! Come forth and do battle!

21:00.530 --> 21:03.660
You blithering fools! Do you 
not see who is before you?

21:03.660 --> 21:06.180
Shogun!

21:06.180 --> 21:07.240
Welcome!

21:09.900 --> 21:13.510
<i>All the customers who come 
in the middle of a DVD</i>

21:13.510 --> 21:15.910
<i>are met with this menacing scowl.</i>

21:16.760 --> 21:18.280
<i>How unreasonable.</i>

21:20.750 --> 21:23.230
There are too many customers lately.

21:23.230 --> 21:24.970
I wish there would be less.

21:24.970 --> 21:26.880
Hey, don't say that...

21:27.450 --> 21:31.410
<i>We're getting enough foot traffic 
to make Sabine grouchy.</i>

21:32.090 --> 21:34.350
<i>I'm sure the reason that 
glasses started to sell...</i>

21:34.970 --> 21:37.310
<i>is all thanks to the chancellor!</i>

21:37.310 --> 21:41.050
The customers are happy! 
Which makes me happy, too!

21:41.050 --> 21:43.160
That's a real win-win situation!

21:44.100 --> 21:45.890
<i>Oh, another customer!</i>

21:45.890 --> 21:47.650
Welcome!

21:48.930 --> 21:50.740
Please help me!

22:05.920 --> 22:08.610
<i>I open my eyes, and where do I find myself?</i>

22:10.550 --> 22:13.260
<i>Maybe I should go back to bed</i>

22:15.140 --> 22:17.730
<i>Pretending I'm still half-asleep</i>

22:19.270 --> 22:23.790
<i>Running away from reality, 
to the west and east</i>

22:24.440 --> 22:26.200
<i>To be honest, life's all about</i>

22:26.200 --> 22:28.960
<i>Taking falls and getting back up 
(heavy damage)</i>

22:28.960 --> 22:32.070
<i>Hurt as it may, there's 
still a long road ahead...</i>

22:33.740 --> 22:36.530
<i>Looks like I've reached the end of my rope</i>

22:38.550 --> 22:41.040
<i>Hitting life's harder levels</i>

22:42.830 --> 22:47.400
<i>That's a test from the gods 
that I'll take on</i>

22:47.400 --> 22:49.860
<i>First things first, gotta be the economy!</i>

22:49.860 --> 22:52.510
<i>Aiming for the bourgeois life</i>

22:52.510 --> 22:54.260
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:54.260 --> 22:57.160
<i>No matter what enemies may come my way</i>

22:57.160 --> 22:59.220
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:59.220 --> 23:01.760
<i>I'll get them on my side</i>

23:01.760 --> 23:03.820
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

23:03.820 --> 23:06.360
<i>Who doesn't need money, after all?</i>

23:06.360 --> 23:11.070
<i>To the days where you need to 
scrape by one way or another</i>

23:11.070 --> 23:18.540
<i>Here's to you!</i>
